      "message": "Gemini review (I haven\u0027t reviewed the locking in this file, so check to see if this is correct):\n\n\n*   **Missing Hardware Lock:** \n    In the existing driver code, `cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg()` is called within a critical section that locks physical flash operations (as seen in `flash_get_status` and `flash_set_status` using `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage()`). \n    Your new function, `flash_control_register_locked`, calls `cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg()` *without* acquiring this lock. If this function is invoked while the mapped storage is being accessed elsewhere, it could lead to SPI bus contention or a race condition. \n    **Recommendation:** Wrap the status register read with the appropriate lock/unlock mechanism, or ensure it is explicitly documented that the caller must hold the mapped storage lock.",
